# Branch gate

Pre-implementation workspace check for `{{ input.current_branch }}`.

{% if not input.dirty %}
## Workspace is CLEAN — auto-proceed

The workspace has no uncommitted changes. The host MUST complete this
gate immediately with `decision=proceed` and an empty note. Do NOT
stop or ask the user.

```bash
LOOM=~/.kiro/skills/home/loomv2/scripts/loom.sh
$LOOM output init "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task branch-gate
$LOOM output add  "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task branch-gate \
    --set decision=proceed --set-json 'note=""'
```

branch-create will then create `{{ input.proposed_branch }}` and
implementation proceeds on it.
{% else %}
## Workspace is DIRTY — STOP and ask the user

Current branch: `{{ input.current_branch }}`
Proposed feature branch: `{{ input.proposed_branch }}`

Uncommitted changes:

```
{{ input.status_tail }}
```

The host MUST stop and ask the user how to proceed. Options:

1. User cleans up first (stash / commit / discard — user or host runs
   the git commands the user asks for), then `decision=proceed`.
2. Proceed carrying the dirty changes onto the new feature branch
   (`git checkout -b` preserves the working tree): `decision=proceed`
   with a note saying so.
3. `decision=abort` — the run stops (BLOCKED).

Record the choice:

```bash
LOOM=~/.kiro/skills/home/loomv2/scripts/loom.sh
$LOOM output init "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task branch-gate
$LOOM output add  "{{ input.__loom.workdir }}" --task branch-gate \
    --set decision=<proceed|abort> --set note='<what was done>'
```
{% endif %}
